  "details": "On latest build that was released on Valentine's Day the particle throw system I have on my avatar and stream broke. Best way I can describe it is that you only see one frame of the particle emitter (see clip for visual). Either its just broken and doesn't show more or it clips of the mesh/rendering if it gets to close to the avatar. It is only in the local camera that this is happening in! All other people in the world can see it fine and even other cameras can see it. Another friend has the same particle thing and they have the same bug that their own camera (local) is having it broken too. Kinda annoying given it's an asset for the stream viewers to redeem and they can't even see it in the camera :(\n\nNo exact way to reproduce given I'm not good with particles, but it is an emitter that throws a ball mesh at the avatar. Clip shows it. Given it works everywhere else but local camera I doubt it's anything wrong with the particle system itself. But I will provide link here to the asset: https://foomaring.gumroad.com/l/lmrjbl\n\nAnd here is the clip from my stream showing the bug in action: https://clips.twitch.tv/PeacefulMoralStingray4Head-By-AZz-cgQ8mX9h-\n\nFirst few seconds you see the balls just disappear when they get to close to me. Again this is only in my local camera, as you can see when I switch to first person they are back. I have tested it with friend and it is ONLY local camera this is happening!",
